<div class="calc-content-prose">
  <h2>How to Plan and Estimate Drywall Materials</h2>
  <p>
    Accurately estimating drywall ensures you have enough material to complete tape, mud, and texture without running short or buying costly excess panels:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Measure Perimeter and Height:</strong> Measure the height and linear width of each wall in the room. For rectangular spaces, perimeter is <code>2 × (Length + Width)</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Calculate Ceilings Separately:</strong> Ceilings should always be hung before walls. Calculate ceiling area as <code>Length × Width</code> and add it to your wall area.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose Sheet Dimensions:</strong> Standard 4′ × 8′ sheets are easiest for DIY handling, while 4′ × 12′ sheets minimize vertical butt joints in large open areas and high ceilings.</li>
  </ol>

